---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Known issues — devjoe Garmin" description="Known platform boundaries and product issues for Burnished Sky Ahead.">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Transparent boundaries</p>
      <h1>Known issues</h1>
      <p class="lede">No confirmed product defects are currently published. These Garmin platform boundaries can affect what appears on the watch.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="content-grid">
      <aside>Platform notes</aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Weather freshness</h2>
        <p>Weather availability depends on Garmin’s cached data, the paired phone, account setup, permissions, and synchronization.</p>
        <h2>Weather labels</h2>
        <p>Garmin may omit location metadata. Burnished Sky Ahead avoids exposing coordinates and shows only the current condition caption or an honest weather fallback.</p>
        <h2>Forecast availability</h2>
        <p>Garmin may omit hourly rows or individual values. Burnished Sky Ahead keeps those values visibly unknown and does not invent a forecast.</p>
        <h2>Alarm detail</h2>
        <p>Connect IQ can report an alarm count on supported devices, but it does not expose the next alarm time, repeat rule, weekday, or Smart Wake state.</p>
        <h2>Precipitation detail</h2>
        <p>Garmin supplies one general precipitation chance rather than separate rain and snow probabilities, and does not expose snow accumulation depth here.</p>
        <h2>Always-on display</h2>
        <p>Device sleep settings may turn off AOD independently of the watch face’s AOD design.</p>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a class="button" href="https://github.com/devjoe/devjoe-garmin-site/issues">Review public issues</a>
          <a class="button" href="/burnished-sky-ahead/support/">Troubleshooting</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
